; worldback.eval — a dungeon with TWO ways in (Michael, 2026-09-09).
;
; The crypt's front gate and its back way open the SAME dungeon from different
; places on the world map, and land on different floors of it. What this is
; really checking is that the two are not secretly one:
;
;   - the back way lands on crypt2 at 10,6, NOT on crypt1 where the gate leads;
;   - walking out of the FRONT gate surfaces at the gate even though the party
;     came in by the back — an exit knows its own door;
;   - coming out of a door DISCOVERS it, which is how a back way is found from
;     the inside.
logecho on
reset
leave

; --- in by the BACK way: a different level, a different cell -----------------
discover crypt_back
enter crypt_back
state
mapinfo
pos
world

; --- out by the FRONT: a different door than the one we came in by -----------
leave crypt_gate
world
